    "title": "What is Nowruz? Persian New Year and spring arrive Friday",
    "text": "MICHIGANMichigan Iranian Americans celebrate Persian New Year. When it starts? Jenna PrestininziDetroit Free PressMarch 19, 2026, 11:32 a.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storyPersian and Kurdish communities across Michigan are preparing to welcome in the Persian New Year Friday, March 20.Nowruz, the Persian New Year, start sat 10:46 a.m. on Friday, March 20, aligning with the vernal equinox, celebrating the hope and renewal of spring's arrival, according to the United Nations. The holiday is celebrated in Iran, as well as other countries throughout the Balkans, Caucasus, Middle East and Central Asia, and among communities globally.",
